course: dictionary
lesson: 4023
title: The many meanings of gather
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word gather has more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. Look at the context first. «Hammerhead sharks ... some gather in big schools near islands» means that the sharks come together as a group.
explain: «A telescope gathers much more light than your eye» uses gather in a different way. A telescope does not invite anything to come together. It collects light, so gather here means collect. Ask yourself: what is being gathered, and from where?
explain: Gather can also mean to understand from what you heard, as in «I gather you are new». Gather speed means to slowly get more speed. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Gather is a verb: gather, gathers, gathered, gathering.
fact: To gather means to come together in one place as a group, as in «Almost every culture gathers people together».
fact: To gather things means to collect them from different places, and bees gather nectar from flowers.
fact: To gather can mean to understand from what you heard, and to gather speed or strength means to slowly get more of it.
fact: A good check is to swap in a simpler word, like collect or come together, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Hammerhead sharks ... some gather in big schools near islands.» What does gather mean here? | Throw away | Dive deep under the sea | *Come together as a group | Stand still and quiet
exercise: «A telescope gathers much more light than your eye.» What does gathers mean here? | Blinks | Shouts at | Hides from | *Collects
exercise: Ayo says, «I gather you are new here.» What does gather mean? | *Understand from what you heard | Pick up from the floor | Race forward | Come together in one place
test: «Crows gather in winter roosts.» In this sentence, gather means: | Lift up | Stop singing | Fly away from | *Come together as a group
test: The train began to gather speed as it left the station. What does gather speed mean? | Lose its wheels | Come together at the station | *Slowly get more speed | Stop completely
exam: Which is the best way to check the meaning of gather in «Almost every culture gathers people together»? | Look only at the word before gather | *Swap in a simpler word like "brings together" and see if the sentence still makes sense | Skip the whole sentence and never read it again | Guess that it means happy
